{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            if (s.length() == 1) {\n                char c = s.charAt(0);\n                out.println(isSpecial(c) ? 1 : 0);\n            } else {\n                if (!s.contains(\"X\")) {\n                    out.println(evaluate(s));\n                } else {\n                    int total = 0;\n                    for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {\n                        total += evaluate(replaceX(s, (char) ('0' + d)));\n                    }\n                    out.println(total);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private static boolean isSpecial(char c) {\n        return c == '0' || c == '_' || c == 'X';\n    }\n\n    private static String replaceX(String s, char replacement) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\n            sb.append(c == 'X' ? replacement : c);\n        }\n        return sb.toString();\n    }\n\n    public static int evaluate(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        int ways = (s.charAt(0) == '0') ? 0 : 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            }\n        }\n        int divisible = 0;\n        char a = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        char b = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        if (a == '_' && b == '_') {\n            divisible = 4;\n        } else if (b == '_') {\n            if (a == '0' || a == '5' || a == '2' || a == '7') {\n                divisible = 1;\n            }\n        } else if (a == '_') {\n            if (b == '0' || b == '5') {\n                divisible = 2;\n            }\n        } else {\n            int num = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(n - 2));\n            divisible = (num % 25 == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        return ways * divisible;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            out.println(solve(s));\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private static long solve(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        \n        // Check for leading zero issues\n        if (s.charAt(0) == '0' && n > 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        \n        // Count number of X's and positions of _\n        int xCount = 0;\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\n            if (c == 'X') xCount++;\n        }\n        \n        long total = 0;\n        \n        // Try all possible digits for X (0-9)\n        for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {\n            String replaced = replaceX(s, (char) ('0' + d));\n            \n            // Check if the first character would be '0' with leading zero issue\n            if (replaced.charAt(0) == '0' && n > 1) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            \n            total += countWays(replaced);\n        }\n        \n        return total;\n    }\n    \n    private static String replaceX(String s, char replacement) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\n            sb.append(c == 'X' ? replacement : c);\n        }\n        return sb.toString();\n    }\n    \n    private static long countWays(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        long ways = 1;\n        \n        // Count ways for underscores in positions other than last two\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    ways *= 9; // Can't be 0 for first digit\n                } else {\n                    ways *= 10; // Can be any digit\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Check divisibility by 25 based on last two digits\n        char last1 = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        char last2 = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        \n        int divisibleCount = 0;\n        \n        if (last2 == '_' && last1 == '_') {\n            // Both last two digits are unknown\n            divisibleCount = 4; // 00, 25, 50, 75\n        } else if (last2 == '_') {\n            // Only second last digit is unknown\n            if (last1 == '0') {\n                divisibleCount = 2; // 00, 50\n            } else if (last1 == '5') {\n                divisibleCount = 2; // 25, 75\n            } else {\n                divisibleCount = 0;\n            }\n        } else if (last1 == '_') {\n            // Only last digit is unknown\n            if (last2 == '0') {\n                divisibleCount = 1; // 00\n            } else if (last2 == '2') {\n                divisibleCount = 1; // 25\n            } else if (last2 == '5') {\n                divisibleCount = 1; // 50\n            } else if (last2 == '7') {\n                divisibleCount = 1; // 75\n            } else {\n                divisibleCount = 0;\n            }\n        } else {\n            // Both last two digits are known\n            int num = (last2 - '0') * 10 + (last1 - '0');\n            divisibleCount = (num % 25 == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        \n        return ways * divisibleCount;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0001438752660760656, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -3.1470757676288486e-05, -2.884823152271565e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.4638240878121e-06, -0.0004204819560982287, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.184158387943171e-05, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -2.5